{"title":"Career Roadmap · FF&E Specialist","role":"FF&E Specialist","summary":"An FF&E (Furniture, Fixtures & Equipment) Specialist manages the selection, specification, documentation, procurement coordination and installation of furniture, lighting, decorative fixtures, equipment and other interior elements for commercial, hospitality, residential, workplace and institutional projects.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Arch (Bachelor of Architecture)","Course":"Interior Architecture & Design"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An FF&E (Furniture, Fixtures & Equipment) Specialist manages the selection, specification, documentation, procurement coordination and installation of furniture, lighting, decorative fixtures, equipment and other interior elements for commercial, hospitality, residential, workplace and institutional projects."},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Arch graduate, the strongest positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Interior Architecture","Materials","Furniture","Product Specification","Procurement","Documentation","Project Coordination"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The role sits between design and project delivery."},{"type":"p","text":"A strong FF&E professional needs to understand not only what looks good, but also:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Dimensions"},{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Durability"},{"text":"Fire and safety requirements"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Maintenance"},{"text":"Cost"},{"text":"Lead times"},{"text":"Vendor capabilities"},{"text":"Installation"},{"text":"Project schedules"},{"text":"Procurement constraints"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Career Flow"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Arch","Interior Design + Building Materials","Furniture + Lighting + Materials Knowledge","Interior Documentation","FF&E Specification","Product Research + Vendor Coordination","BOQ / Schedules / Costing"